TEXT -728 -32 Left 5 ;The generator is switched to the isolated network\nAfter 5s the speed controller is set to a fix value\nAfter 8s the bus is shorted \nThe maximum short circuit current at start of fault is\nvery high and the steady state current is much lower\n \nThe maximal short circuit current is limited by the \ntransformer (see also SG_IsolatedOperation_ShortCircuit2.asc\nfor direct short on the terminals of the generator)\n \n \nHINT: If the speed controller is not limited \nthe short circuit current is only a little bit higher- > test it\nQuestion: Can the frequency be stabilized if speed controller\nis not limited -> test it without limit and longer simulation \ntime intervall (20s)\n \nNOTE: The generator current is mainly inductive (because\nof transformer) so the load angle is about zero. \nIf the generator is shorted at 20kV the current will be ohmic\nand so the load angle is about 90 degrees. See this \nat SG_IsolatedOperation_ShortCircuit2.asc
