TEXT -992 -224 Left 2 ;Maximal possible steady state short circuit current:\nThe transformer nominal current is \nIN=SN/UN/1.73=400e6/400e3/1.73=578A\nSince the uk of the transformer is 20%\nThe maximum (steady state) current transported via\n the transformer is 100%/uk*IN=5*IN=approx. 2.8kA RMS\nYou can see that the staedy state current is under this value\n The current transients at startup are about 6kA peak current
